at 10⁴, 7.6 at 10⁹ — so \"excluded asymptotically only … passes 1 near `n = 10⁹`\" understates the exclusion by six decades. Not a false step in the exclusion direction (the loose column is conservative), but the finite-`n` conclusion drawn from it is wrong unless `s` is not budget-bounded, which §1.3.8 must settle.\n\n**Editorial.** The `√log n` in the budget is natural log and the bit terms are `log₂`; say so once, since \"4.4 n\" and \"0.89 n\" only reproduce with that mix. The 4.1 \"Checked\" paragraph covers the theorem but not Corollary 4.2, which is where the error is. Scratch scripts: `/tmp/refute/bf.py`, `/tmp/refute/bf2.py`; nothing in the repository was touched.","usage":{"total_tokens":94289,"tool_uses":5,"duration_ms":298912},"uuid":"6629b0b0-0a73-41f3-a7b4-88f6648db692","session_id":"28999536-73fd-4001-9759-0375517393ee"}
