, the segment width","+`g log₂(n/g) ≈ 1.44 · n √log n · 2^{−√log n}` must be at most","+`s^{9/10} ≤ B_p^{9/10}`, i.e. `2^{−√log n} ≤ n^{−1/10} (log n)^{−0.05}`","+up to constants, which fails for large `n` since `√log n = o(log n)`","+— but only for very large `n`. The arithmetic (`gap_table`; the ratio","+is the segment width over `B_p^{9/10}` at the smallest fitting `g`,","+with the verified route's `g` beside it for comparison):"," ","-| `n` | budget, bits | `g/n` | segment width | `s^{9/10}` | ratio |","-|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| 125 | 111 | 0.20 | 58 | 157 | 0.37 |","-| 10³ | 704 | 0.23 | 485 | 1,200 | 0.41 |","-| 10⁴ | 6,160 | 0.24 | 4,940 | 10,800 | 0.46 |","-| 10⁶ | 5.39 × 10⁵ | 0.25 | 5.02 × 10⁵ | 8.19 × 10⁵ | 0.61 |","-| 10⁹ | 4.95 × 10⁸ | 0.26 | 5.06 × 10⁸ | 4.92 × 10⁸ | 1.03 |","+| `n` | verified `B_v/n` | its `g/n` | paper `B_p/n` | its `g/n` | segment width | `B_p^{9/10}` | ratio |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 125 | 0.89 | 0.20 | 2.20 | 0.080 | 36.5 | 157 | 0.23 |","+| 10³ | 0.70 | 0.23 | 2.63 | 0.060 | 242 | 1,200 | 0.20 |","+| 10⁶ | 0.54 | 0.25 | 3.72 | 0.028 | 1.44 × 10⁵ | 8.19 × 10⁵ | 0.18 |","+| 10⁹ | 0.50 | 0.26 | 4.55 | 0.016 | 9.4 × 10⁷ | 4.92 × 10⁸ | 0.19 |","+| 10¹⁵ | 0.47 | 0.27 | 5.88 | 0.006 | 4.6 × 10¹³ | 1.56 × 10¹⁴ | 0.29 |","+| 10²¹ | 0.46 | 0.27 | 6.95 | 0.003 | 2.5 × 10¹⁹ | 4.6 × 10¹⁹ | 0.55 |","+| 10²⁴ | 0.46 | 0.27 | 7.43 | 0.002 | 1.9 × 10²² | 2.4 × 10²² | 0.78 |"," "," So the paper route is excluded for this family **asymptotically only**:","-the ratio passes 1 near `n = 10⁹`, and below that the arithmetic","-alone does not exclude a coarse chain — with the caveat that Theorem","-D.1's constants are unknown (§1.3.8), so nothing is claimed at any","-finite `n` in either direction. The budget `n √log n/(log log n)²` is","-itself below `n` until `n ≈ 10⁹`, which is the same fact: the verified","-exponent is `o(n)` only in the limit.","+the ratio is below 1 at every `n` up to `10²⁴` and passes it beyond,","+so at any size one could write down the arithmetic alone does not","+exclude a coarse chain on the paper route — with the caveat that","+Theorem D.1's constants are unknown (§1.3.8), so nothing is claimed at","+any finite `n` in either direction. (The first draft mixed the routes,","+taking `g` from the verified budget and the width against `s = B_p`,","+and put the crossover near `10⁹`; the refuter caught the mix.) The","+verified budget `B_v` is itself below `n` at every `n` in the table,","+which is the same fact: the verified exponent is `o(n)` only in the","+limit."," "," **What the lemma does not cover.** A certificate that is not a coarse"," chain at all — one whose satisfying assignments do not determine any"]},{"oldStart":1414,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1440,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | maximum degree 3 | NP-hard (MS 1988, not held) | the acyclic orientation is a relaxation, not a certificate (55% of orientations disagree, 64% of optimal ones unforced, to 7 vertices); the residual is `F_k` | **no** |"," | cocomparability, AT-free | NP-hard, `= tw` | contain the doubles at blow-up 2: fit iff all graphs fit | **no**, by §4.1 |"," | chordal, starlike, clique-tree covers | NP-hard (Gustedt 4.1, 4.3); block graphs polynomial | twins consecutive (Thm 4.4), `O*(2^u)`; a chain over the centre; `α₀ ≤ √n` is NP-hard and `2^{O(√n)}` by Gustedt 6.4 (Cor. 4.5) | **no**: the chain over the units; the `√n` subclass is the blow-up, not a certificate |","-| any chain-carrying certificate at spacing `g` | — | `N ≥ n log₂(n/(eg))` (Lemma 4.6) | **no** on the verified route at every `n`; on the paper route asymptotically |","+| any chain-carrying certificate at spacing `g` | — | `N ≥ n log₂(n/(eg)) − 1` (Lemma 4.6) | **no** on the verified route at every `n ≥ 16`; on the paper route asymptotically (crossover beyond `10²⁴`) |"," "," **Plan §0.6, item 04's kill: met.** No class on which pathwidth is"," NP-hard has `O(n)`-bit layouts under bounded-width constraints, nor a"]},{"oldStart":1448,"