{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgicJrB1VkYUsvQe7GznY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 04 is done; nothing further is pending. Eight items remain unchecked, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line was added, and nothing was committed, per the driver's rules.\n\n**Outcome.** No NP-hard class among the five has `O(n)`-bit layouts under bounded-width constraints, so item 04's kill criterion is met and item 09 becomes the chain-count attempt only. Each class presents the same object in disguise: a chain through the lattice `F_k`.\n\n**What §4 of `reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` establishes, each proved and checked on every graph to 7 vertices with zero failures:**\n- **Cobipartite.** Some optimal layout places one clique entirely first, and the decision is then a one-sided cut condition on a chain of subsets of the other side. On the doubles from item 03 that lattice is `F_k` verbatim, so cobipartite pathwidth is item 05's lattice problem with no translation. Side remark: exact `vs` in `O*(2^{max(a,b)})`.\n- **Split.** Polynomial, so moot. Gustedt's Lemma 2.8 and paper 2's criterion are on record; I added the layout-side proof and an exhaustive check on every split partition.\n- **Maximum degree 3.** The one `O(n)`-bit object, the acyclic orientation, does not determine the value: 55% of orientations on subcubic atlas graphs have disagreeing linear extensions.\n- **Cocomparability and AT-free.** Contain the cobipartite doubles at blow-up 2, so they fit iff all graphs fit.\n- **Chordal, starlike, clique-tree covers.** A twin lemma gives `vs` in `O*(2^u)` over twin classes. Combined with Gustedt's Theorem 6.4, starlike graphs with centre at most `√n` form an NP-hard class on which pathwidth is `2^{O(√n)}` unconditionally. The report says plainly this is the quadratic blow-up seen from the algorithm's side, not an answer to Q.\n- **Gap lemma.** Any certificate carrying the layout's prefix sets at spacing `g` needs `n log₂(n/(eg)) − 1` bits. This excludes the family on the verified route at every `n ≥ 16`, and on the paper route only asymptotically, with the crossover beyond `10²⁴`.\n\n**The refuter subagent** (1 of 4 used) found two wrong sentences and two gaps, no wrong verdict: Corollary 4.2's index range, the twin induction order, Lemma 4.6's missing uniformity hypothesis, and a mix of the two budgets in the gap table. All are fixed, and the corrected corollary is now checked directly on all 3,653 (partition, k) decisions.\n\n**Bookkeeping.** Gate PASS (1,948 tests, pathwidth_solver 123, 0 sorry, no axiom). PROGRESS.md has the iteration 4 section and reads 4/12; item 04 is marked `[x]`. New files: `learning/subexp_classes.py`, `tests/test_subexp_classes.py` (10 tests), `reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/04_classes/`. No instance was run and `solutions/` is untouched."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":229195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":678,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":787,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28999536-73fd-4001-9759-0375517393ee","uuid":"1753acc8-6d82-4d8f-953d-1011b1bb4ed2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:37:28.744Z","request_id":"req_011CgicJqpRxzCh7jDxJe6qP"}
